WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:02.752
I know something you don't know.

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:04.838
Oh, yeah? 
What's that?

00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:07.382
You are absolutely going to be

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:09.050
what's best for her.

00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:15.515
Writing and publishing this book 

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.766
was a long journey.

00:00:16.766 --> 00:00:18.184
I actually came up with the idea

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.311
all the way back in 2003.

00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:22.564
I was really interested
in the Enron trial.

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:24.733
I am telling you, Owen
is not that guy.

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.609
You’re starting to sound 
like most wives

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:29.529
whose husbands have been 
accused of white-collar crime.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.115
I started to imagine a woman
who found herself between who

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:35.368
she thought her husband was,
and who the world thought he was.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.370
And in 2016,

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.622
after I gave birth 
to my first child,

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:42.542
I was able to find the story
I was hoping to tell.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.712
You know, I was a little like 
you when I was your age.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.006
Which is about someone 
becoming a mother.

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:50.508
And that's the book that 
we are turning into

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:51.843
this wonderful series.

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:53.178
So where is he, Hannah?

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:54.512
Where's my dad?

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:56.723
He's going to have an 
explanation, you know he will.

00:00:57.849 --> 00:00:59.601
The Last Thing He Told Me, 

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:00.852
people will be thrilled with

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:02.103
if they're fans of the book.

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:05.815
Laura Dave has thought
through every possible choice.

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:07.609
She knows what she wants
to put on the screen.

00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:09.694
My husband, Josh,

00:01:09.694 --> 00:01:12.906
and I knew that we wanted
to write the show together.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.366
And the beauty of 
a television show

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:16.826
is that you can be expansive

00:01:16.826 --> 00:01:19.037
and spend more time
with these characters,

00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:21.623
and up the propulsion
of what’s happening to them.

00:01:22.123 --> 00:01:24.292
Like all of Laura's great fiction,

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:26.336
not only is there a great drive,

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:28.755
there's also this real heart
underneath it.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.925
The best television
operates on multiple levels,

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.218
and I think this does that.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.428
I may not know why your
father did what he did, 

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.763
but I know who he is.

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:39.557
I love Laura Dave's writing.

00:01:39.682 --> 00:01:43.144
It's not very often that I feel
I have to do something.

00:01:43.144 --> 00:01:44.604
I just have to do it.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.565
I wrote letters to everyone 
involved about why

00:01:47.565 --> 00:01:50.401
I would really love the 
opportunity to play Hannah Hall.

00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:52.737
The letter brought tears to my eyes.

00:01:52.737 --> 00:01:55.740
She connected so 
wholeheartedly to this character,

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.243
and we really knew
she was meant to play her.

00:01:58.243 --> 00:01:59.452
Have you seen a teenage girl?

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.287
Sixteen, blond, pink streaks.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:04.499
Writing the book, Hannah
was sort of amorphous in my mind.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:06.876
Now, when I reread the book,

00:02:06.876 --> 00:02:09.337
it's Jen's face, and it 
will always be Jen's face.

00:02:09.337 --> 00:02:11.214
She is Hannah Hall to me.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.049
What could you possibly
say right now

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:14.551
that would make any sense?

00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:16.010
I don't know.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.470
He lied to me.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.097
He lied to me, too.

00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:21.182
Even for people who have read it,

00:02:21.182 --> 00:02:24.769
we are trying to 
hone Laura's incredible

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:27.647
book into something 
vivid and alive, 

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.982
but also surprising.

00:02:29.274 --> 00:02:30.942
When I read her book, I was just amazed

00:02:30.942 --> 00:02:32.485
how tight the story is.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.821
We want to show to be 
the same kind of thing

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.990
where you go, “I got 
to see the next episode.”

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:39.534
Everyone just really 
brought their A-game,

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.703
bringing the show together 
in a way that

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:43.163
it's beyond my wildest dreams.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.623
You said that people don't 
run for no reason.

00:02:45.748 --> 00:02:47.625
Hannah, you need to 
get out of there now.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.131
I thought that part of 
my life was over.

